_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:dc63c96eae31df2bacee3e62c30d57d12e9c4b64ccab921815b73c68fc96bb1d","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:14:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T10:14:30Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m138-v0.13.8/m13stage8-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m138-v0.13.8","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m138-v0.13.8","body":"# Engacer OS M13.8 / 0.13.8 - Settings, errors and recovery\n\nThis release qualifies the named Settings/search/feedback and display tasks within M13-STAGE8-VM-v1. M13.9-M13.12 and final integration remain separate. [Install](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/docs/handbook/install-m138.md), [find and change settings](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/docs/handbook/settings-m138.md), [decisions and retained finishing items](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/docs/milestones/m13-8.md).\n\n## Download and verify\n\nExtract the complete VMware ZIP, open EngacerOS.vmx and choose I Copied It if asked. Its new blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk is not preinstalled. Keep the shipped devices enabled, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM, UEFI and Secure Boot off. The release also includes the exact ISO.\n\n- Build: `f909d62ef8a6a2c28b8a7128dc8a3066`.\n- ISO SHA256: `65b920c7ba5d19f15173271724298d6539247666be6061319d5108835cede51f`.\n- VMware ZIP SHA256: `64798e58c8924bb651b25bebe0c9e28e8830f47cb8c814bebf14c425f9865f92`.\n\nTwenty assets include media, maps, exact build/starter manifests, checksums, notices and applicable third-party source/licenses. The build binds 610 compiled inputs.\n\n## What changes\n\nSettings has a fixed current-category search row above five real categories, with readable two-line results. Ctrl+F searches bounded ASCII category names, descriptions and declared aliases such as dark mode, scale, apps and contrast. Results open supported controls. No file index, background worker or invented hardware switch is added. Each window generation owns its temporary query. Clear/category navigation and layered Escape are explicit; a file dialog retains ownership.\n\nAppearance/display retain actual Preview, Apply, Cancel and distribution-default transactions. Input/accessibility remain separately labelled immediate saves. A second Settings window cannot replace another preview; removing an optional app does not remove the desktop or reinstall it when appearance defaults are restored. Invalid saved appearance activates safe defaults and can be replaced by a real Apply.\n\nOrdinary shell feedback prefers the lower workspace and avoids intersecting captions through bounded placement. Drawing and hit testing share one rectangle. Dismiss clears only the message. If every ordinary corner is crowded, the focused caption stays protected. Empty search hints use shared semantic muted colors in Settings and Start. The offline Welcome guide documents the current Settings search.\n\n## Exact native qualification\n\n80 named native task/profile checks bind these media: five full Settings search/display/theme/message journeys, shared-control profiles, complete preview/save/cancel/default/input and optional-app tasks, semantic-invalid preference recovery, dirty-document/dialog/conflict/USB feedback and independent starts. The exact enabled-device VMware package installs, restarts with ISO retained and starts twice from disk, with unchanged existing-VM inventory. See [acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/evidence/M13/8/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/evidence/M13/8/resources.json) and [visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/4f8da11c8ef217a9256f0bbfbde52a350e86176e/evidence/M13/8/visual-review.json).\n\nFixed desktop state is 554,844 bytes, +704 bytes for eight bounded query records. Installer state remains 48,412 bytes and font masks remain 251,248 bytes. Completed named tasks retain zero managed pages and idle CPUs halt. Configured RAM, physical framebuffer, fixed state and managed peak/retained pages are separate.\n\nThe host observer caches only immutable symbol locations and disables Nagle on its own QMP client; every mutable guest value is freshly read. This is observation overhead, not native response/FPS evidence. Actual latency/frame qualification remains M13.9.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis is bounded search over supported Settings categories, not arbitrary system or file search. Named VM tasks do not establish a fresh fourteen-controller matrix, universal hardware, vendor GPU 3D or general Windows/DOS compatibility. Agent visual/scenario review is separate from a human novice study. Earlier failed aliases, stale observer expectations and incomplete candidates remain diagnostics, never qualification of these corrected bytes. The M13.10 search-heading/idle-footer/clear-label/plain-error-copy finishing items remain explicitly scheduled before final M13.12. The owner-reported M13.7 long-uptime freeze is under investigation in M13.9, with real-duration final qualification required in M13.12; no fix is claimed here. The optional screensaver remains M13.11 and is not a freeze workaround. Matching GitHub downloads and complete public website closure are separate gates.\n"}